…e “Message”, the other is “Chat_Message”. “Message”is the message that pop up when admin or customer requires to view the order content/when customer place an order.“Chat_Message” is the messages sent through the chat panel in the pattern of email. Therefore, it has two send message usecases (“SendMessageUseCase” and “SendChatMessageUseCase”.)

The methods that can be used are “generate_message_for_admin(Order order)”, “generate_message_for_customer(Order order)
” and “send_chat_message_mail(String user_input, String senderAccount, String receiverAccount, String senderPassword)”. The programmer should provide the arguments required.

The first method “generate_message_for_admin(Order order)” return a formatted String like {"Order details: " + order_id + "\n" + order_date + "\n" + item_list + "\n" + order_status + message_date;}

“generate_message_for_customer(Order order)” returns a formatted String like {"Dear Customer," + "\n" + " We are trying our best to process your order." + "\n" + "Order details: " + order_id + "\n" + order_date + "\n" + item_list + "\n" + order_status + "Thank you for your patience and have a nice day!" + message_date;}

“send_chat_message_mail(String user_input, String senderAccount, String receiverAccount, String senderPassword)” can create and send a email, whose content is user_input, from the senderAccount to receiverAccount. The senderPassword is required for the verification of the senderAccount.

